Subject: find/exec.c: on OpenVMS, run -exec and -ok commands without fork()

OpenVMS has no fork().  launch() runs the command as DCL in a subprocess
instead, through vms_spawn_command() (vms/vms_spawn.c; docs/DECISIONS.md
D1), so DCL verbs and foreign-command symbols work as well as images.
The subprocess starts in our default directory, so for -execdir and
-okdir launch() changes to the file's directory around it and back.
Only the file names are quoted: with "+" the arguments after the
initial ones, with ";" the words that contained {}; the words the user
typed are passed to DCL as they are, so qualifiers and keywords work.
A command line too long for DCL returns 0, as for E2BIG, and
bc_do_exec() tries again with fewer arguments.  launch() stores the
exit code in last_child_status, and -exec ... ; tests it directly: there
is no waitpid() status to decode.

